WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.290
I wanted to talk about this yesterday, but didn't have time.

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:10.739
Last week after weeks and weeks of not taking questions in a press conference, after days of having

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.000
nothing public on his calendar whatsoever, Trump decided to do...

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.320
basically a campaign rally.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.320
He went to Ohio to do a rally in front of a friendly crowd, kind of like what you do when you're running for president.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.219
Supposedly, it was going to be an "Infrastructure" speech,

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:27.570
by the way,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:32.730
how often is it Infrastructure Week? It seems like almost every week in this administration is Infrastructure Week.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.339
Trump went completely and totally off the rails. It turned into a very strange, garbled rant

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:44.099
resembling the English language only loosely, and demonstrating a sort of Sarah Palin like

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:51.959
inability to communicate anything of meaning through language, and it got so bad that the three major cable networks CNN, MSNBC

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.060
and Fox News, all just cut away from the speech, although

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.800
you'll be pleased to know that good old Fox Business Network stayed with the entire thing all the way through.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.780
Here is Fox bailing, when it got weird. Former George  W. Bush('s)

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.049
White House Press Secretary, Dana Perino, who's now a Fox News anchor, fittingly,

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:14.999
explaining that they are going away, and she looked sort of in physical pain as she said it.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.209
[President Trump:]  32,000 soldiers... [Dana Perino:] Alright you've been watching President Trump, who is in Ohio giving a speech, a wide-ranging speech,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:27.239
but mostly focusing on his infrastructure plan, and former White House Deputy Chief of Staff [during George W. Bush administration], Karl Rove is back with me.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.710
I like that "wide-ranging" is code for "Trump is all over the place, real quick

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:37.139
go to Karl Rove to try to save us,  save us here." So even Fox cutting away even though

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.650
they did stay with it a few minutes longer than CNN and MSNBC.

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:46.859
So here are just random weird moments, the entire speech was totally off the rails, all right. Here's just a

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.600
random 20 seconds of Trump from the speech. [Trump:] Where a very important,

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:54.539
and respected,

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:57.119
in some circles,  Democrat,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:04.120
said we want to get rid, we should get rid of our Second Amendment, in other words, get rid of it. That's really, ah,

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.940
[inaudible comment from audience], yeah,

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.860
[you] could be right about that!

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.760
So we're going to protect our Second Amendment. That's not going to happen. We have the best judges,

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:23.520
we put on a tremendous amount of great federal District Court Judges, will be setting records,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.520
we are setting records,

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.550
appeals court judges, uh,

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.860
Supreme Court judge,

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.100
fantastic,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.100
Justice Gorsuch,

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.000
What is he talking about setting records like what, what the hell is this guy on?

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:44.770
Just another few seconds from Trump's bizarre speech that networks couldn't even stay with: ...and we didn't have one Democrat who voted

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.170
for that. they want to raise your taxes and

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.690
they want people to come in from

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.870
the border, and they want,

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.490
I guess,

00:02:54.490 --> 00:03:01.839
want? I can't imagine they want, but certainly drugs are flowing across borders. We need walls, we started building our wall,

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.190
I'm so proud of it. We started, we started, we have 1.6. billion,

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:13.329
and we've already started, you saw the pictures yesterday, I said what a thing of beauty, and on September 28th,

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.790
we go further... Yeah, that was a lie, by the way, the pictures

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.209
he's referring to, were from the replacement of 2 miles of border fence,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.730
dating back to the 1990s.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.500
Uh, we've got one more clip, again,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:30.700
just disjointed rantings of a madman. We spent, and I was against it from the beginning, they try and say, "well

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.790
maybe not". I

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.360
was

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.869
against it from the beginning, and by the way,

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.813
we're knocking the hell out of ISIS, we'll

00:03:36.813 --> 00:03:40.750
be coming out of Syria, like very soon. Let the other people take care of it now. [Applause]

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.489
Very soon, very soon. We're coming out. We're gonna have a hundred percent of

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:52.539
The Caliphate, as they call it, sometimes referred to as "land," taking it all back quickly, quickly.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:59.380
Uh, but we're gonna be coming out of there real soon, gonna get back to our country, where we belong, where we want to be.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.179
But just think of it, we spent, as of three months ago,

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.760
seven trillion dollars, not billion, not million.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:17.409
Seven trillion with a "T"! Nobody ever heard of the word trillion until 10 years ago.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:22.300
We spent seven trillion dollars in the Middle East.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.300
We'd build a school they'd blow it up, we'd build it again, they'd blow it up, we'd build it again...

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.480
Hasn't been blown up yet, but it will be.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:39.190
But if we want a school in Ohio, to fix the windows, you can't get the money. If you want a school in

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.650
Pennsylvania or Iowa, to get federal money, you can't get the money.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:50.380
We spent seven trillion dollars in the Middle East, and you know we have for it? Nothing!

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.619
Remember I used to say, "keep the oil",

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.820
as a civilian!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:05:01.719
I used to say, did anybody hear me say that? That's before I decided to go on this journey with all of you,

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.620
I got tired of watching.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.760
What on earth is this guy talking about? I, it is the

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.920
disjointed rantings of someone who understands nothing. It's always

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:19.809
Infrastructure Week or Month, or whatever. Nothing actually happens except Trump just showing up and talking about his random, random musings here, and

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.770
it's, there's two phases of a Trump speech:

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:30.940
there's the horrible syntax of the teleprompter-reading, where he's looking off at an angle, and saying, "and

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.620
if we were to...

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.679
become a better nation of, and

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.589
then we would...".  Right?  It's like it's just he can't read it,

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:42.880
it just makes no sense, whatsoever, and then you see when he shifts off the teleprompter and

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:48.429
looks straight ahead, and, but then you don't even know what the guy's talking about, because he's just completely off the rails, and

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.630
improvising, and I hope that soon we actually get a press conference, supposedly, he's doing one today, uh,

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.940
questions like, uh, Mr. President, can you just say, definitively, did you have sex with stormy Daniels?

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:04.179
Did you realize that your people were knowingly and directly dealing with Russian intelligence officers?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:11.140
Did you know about the hundred and thirty thousand dollars that Michael Cohen paid Stormy Daniels? Have you reimbursed? Some specific

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:16.960
questions, and you, you can't put him out there because he could end up saying something horribly self-incriminating.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.299
So I hope we get a press conference soon. These

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:23.710
speeches are but so bizarre that even Fox News had to cut away from it.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.789
Even if he did get those questions though, I think he would go off on a tangent about how he won the

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.270
2016 election; it was greatest victory of all times.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.050
Something like that to deflect.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:38.500
Maybe he would, but I think he would very likely end up saying something totally, totally self incriminating, and it's pretty clear

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.030
they're trying to keep him away from those types of questions.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:43.180
Hopefully he will get some today.

